WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.153
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.153 --> 00:00:02.629
- [Voiceover] Tootsie
Rolls seem simple enough.

00:00:02.629 --> 00:00:04.200
That piece of gooey chocolate wrapped

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:06.236
up in a perfect little bite.

00:00:06.236 --> 00:00:07.240
But believe it or not,

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.160
these tasty treats saved the lives

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:11.905
of U.S. Marines in the Korean War.

00:00:11.905 --> 00:00:13.822
- [Male Voice] So good.

00:00:14.942 --> 00:00:17.581
- [Voiceover] In 1950, at the
North Korean Chosin Reservoir,

00:00:17.581 --> 00:00:20.460
U.S. Marine troops were engaged in battle.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:21.901
The Marines were running
out of ammunition,

00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:25.239
and called for an airdrop
of 60mm mortar rounds.

00:00:25.239 --> 00:00:29.508
Code name for these bullets? Tootsie Roll.

00:00:29.508 --> 00:00:31.337
When the supplies fell from the sky,

00:00:31.337 --> 00:00:33.388
troops were surprised to find boxes filled

00:00:33.388 --> 00:00:35.548
with the actual candies.

00:00:35.548 --> 00:00:37.247
- [Male Voice] Where are the bullets?

00:00:37.247 --> 00:00:38.112
- [Voiceover] This fluke turned out

00:00:38.112 --> 00:00:40.020
to be a blessing in disguise.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:42.946
Freezing cold temperatures had
cracked vehicle fuel lines,

00:00:42.946 --> 00:00:44.931
leaving troops stranded.

00:00:44.931 --> 00:00:46.848
And although the candies were frozen,

00:00:46.848 --> 00:00:49.586
they softened easily in
the mouths of servicemen.

00:00:49.586 --> 00:00:50.486
- [Male Voice] Mmm, so good.

00:00:50.486 --> 00:00:51.597
- [Voiceover] Marines quickly realized

00:00:51.597 --> 00:00:52.597
they could melt the candies down

00:00:52.597 --> 00:00:55.130
to a putty and seal the broken pipes.

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:56.255
- [Male Voice] Good as new!

00:00:56.255 --> 00:00:57.517
- [Voiceover] When the chocolate refroze,

00:00:57.517 --> 00:00:58.687
they were able to drive to safety

00:00:58.687 --> 00:01:01.056
in their newly functional vehicles.

00:01:01.056 --> 00:01:03.227
The Marines who successfully
escaped the Reservoir

00:01:03.227 --> 00:01:05.688
admit that Tootsie Rolls had
a big hand in their survival,

00:01:05.688 --> 00:01:08.886
and they call themselves the Chosin Few.

00:01:08.886 --> 00:01:12.048
I'd call that a pretty sweet victory.

00:01:12.048 --> 00:01:14.631
(upbeat music)

